    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44045" root="&#xA;                        نعم&#xA;                    " body-key="n1">
                        
                            4
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنْعَمَ عَلَيْهِ بِشَىْءٍِ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>He conferred, or bestowed,
upon him a thing as a favour.</i> See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَحْسَنَ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنْعَمَ عَجْنَهُ</span>
                        <i>He kneaded it well, thoroughly,</i> or
<i>soundly.</i> (TA, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَيْعٌ</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنْعَمَ الدَّقَّ</span>
                        <i>He
bruised</i> or <i>powdered finely:</i> see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَقَّقَ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنْعَمَ</span>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَبْخَهُ</span>
                        <i>He cooked it well;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَجَادَ طَبْخَهُ</span>.
(IbrD.) The verb is often used in this sense.
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنْعَمَ ٱللّٰهُ بِكَ عَيْنًا</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبْغَضَ</span>.

